// Rule: [T1053.005][T1574.002] Teleshim - Feedback Scheduled Task
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1053.005, T1574.002
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Hunting query - campaign-specific artifacts
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR / Microsoft Sentinel with MDE tables
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Campaign-specific persistence through a ten-minute task targeting ProgramData.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for feedback scheduled task using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A match indicates the complete campaign artifact intersection in a process command line.
// A match does not prove: It does not identify task creation through COM/API, prove payload maliciousness or detect changed names, cadence or paths.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Title: TELESHIM Feedback Scheduled Task in ProgramData
// Status: Hunting query - campaign-specific artifacts
// Confidence: High
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR / Microsoft Sentinel with MDE tables
// Telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Hunt for the exact scheduled-task persistence construction observed
// by Zscaler ThreatLabz in the TELESHIM-related campaign.
// ATT&CK: T1053.005, T1574.002
// Limitation: Task name, recurrence and payload path are attacker-controlled.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "schtasks.exe"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "/create"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "/sc minute"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "/mo 10"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "/tn \"Feedback\""
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "/tr"
| where ProcessCommandLine contains @"\ProgramData\"
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, AccountName,
          ProcessCommandLine,
          InitiatingProcessFileName,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
          SHA1, ReportId
